## Headline

kpi 2025 emissions | 22,870 t | -13.7% since 2023 | good
kpi Reduction since 2023 | 3,630 t | -13.7%
kpi Scope 2 change | -54.6% | since 2023 | good
kpi Scope 3 share of total | 86.6% | in 2025 | bad
kpi Still to cut by 2030 | 4,320 t | to reach 18,550 t

Our emissions fell 3,630 tonnes, or 13.7 percent, between 2023 and 2025. Most of that came from electricity: scope 2 fell 54.6 percent as 6 of our 8 sites moved to renewable electricity contracts. Scope 3, the emissions in our supply chain, fell much less and is now 86.6 percent of the total. That is where the real challenge lies.

Our target is a 30 percent cut against 2023 by 2030, which means 18,550 tonnes or lower. From 2025 we still have 4,320 tonnes to go.

